NAME
    gcloud alpha number-registry discovered-ranges describe - gets details of a
        single discovered range resource

SYNOPSIS
    gcloud alpha number-registry discovered-ranges describe
        (DISCOVERED_RANGE : --location=LOCATION) [GCLOUD_WIDE_FLAG ...]

DESCRIPTION
    (ALPHA) Gets details of a single discovered range resource.

EXAMPLES
    To get the details of a single discovered range my-discovered-range run:

        $ gcloud alpha number-registry discovered-ranges describe \
            my-discovered-range --location=global

POSITIONAL ARGUMENTS
     DiscoveredRange resource - Name of the resource The arguments in this
     group can be used to specify the attributes of this resource. (NOTE) Some
     attributes are not given arguments in this group but can be set in other
     ways.

     To set the project attribute:
      ◆ provide the argument discovered_range on the command line with a
        fully specified name;
      ◆ provide the argument --project on the command line;
      ◆ set the property core/project.

     This must be specified.

       DISCOVERED_RANGE
          ID of the discoveredRange or fully qualified identifier for the
          discoveredRange.

          To set the discovered_range attribute:
          ▸ provide the argument discovered_range on the command line.

          This positional argument must be specified if any of the other
          arguments in this group are specified.

       --location=LOCATION
          The location id of the discoveredRange resource.

          To set the location attribute:
          ▸ provide the argument discovered_range on the command line with a
            fully specified name;
          ▸ provide the argument --location on the command line.

GCLOUD WIDE FLAGS
    These flags are available to all commands: --access-token-file, --account,
